      "writtenOn": "2024-06-10T22:10:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So there\u0027s 2 (overlapping) goals:\n\n1. Attribute broadcastIntent() over binder from other processes\n2. Trace the internal state of the BroadcastQueue\n\nThe original intention of this change was for #1. The existing async BroadcastQueue track was really designed for #2. \n\nGiven the different goals, it seems reasonable to still address #1 with the current cl where we emit additional information on the binder thread itself. \n\nI think #2 needs some more discussion about what we want to see in the traces. Especially because there are existing slices and we\u0027d need to understand if/what is redundant. A slightly broader goal for #2 would be to trace a lifecycle  all the way from enqueue to dispatch and receipt in the receiving process. We did something similar for bindService.\n\nwdyt?",
      "parentUuid": "490fb8da_b27b3b66",
      "revId": "35fed9daebfd8f081a679934022aa60bb20ca00d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c7adfc6_908ab548",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java",
