      },
      "lineNbr": 14811,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T00:33:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this function (`broadcastIntentLocked`) is being called by the `broadcastIntentWithFeature` at line 15795 below, I feel it\u0027s covering almost the same range of the code, while the new `broadcastIntent` tag has a little bit more information. From the perfetto trace, it\u0027ll look like the below. Is this really necessary?\n\n```\n[.... broadcastIntent             ....]\n [ .. broadcastIntentLockedTraced ...]\n```",
      "parentUuid": "f27c9389_9f9a8475",
      "revId": "35fed9daebfd8f081a679934022aa60bb20ca00d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "539352fe_09d55284",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 14811,
      "author": {
        "id": 1974290
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T19:59:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While the two tags appear to cover similar regions of code, the broadcastIntent tag provides a fuller picture into what\u0027s happening during a binder transaction since the tag slice is displayed alongside other slices (accomplishing goal #1 from Zim\u0027s comment).\n\nIt would be more difficult to visualize the same contextual information if we were to solely rely on the BroadcastQueue track.\n\nLet me know if I can clarify anything else!",
      "parentUuid": "6c7adfc6_908ab548",
      "revId": "35fed9daebfd8f081a679934022aa60bb20ca00d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
